            "doc": {
              "summary": "Start the command and return an owned handle to it.",
              "body": [
                "The child is spawned and its PID announced before this returns; the caller decides what happens next. Await <a href=\"/cuprum/docs/api/commands/#RunningCommand\"><code>RunningCommand.wait</code></a> for the outcome, deliver a signal with <a href=\"/cuprum/docs/api/commands/#RunningCommand\"><code>RunningCommand.signal</code></a>, or stop the child with <a href=\"/cuprum/docs/api/commands/#RunningCommand\"><code>RunningCommand.terminate</code></a> or <a href=\"/cuprum/docs/api/commands/#RunningCommand\"><code>RunningCommand.kill</code></a>.",
                "The handle owns the child's lifetime. Using it as an <code>async with</code> block settles the run on exit — a child still running is stopped down the same <code>SIGTERM</code>, cancel-grace, <code>SIGKILL</code> path a cancelled <code>run()</code> takes — so a caller cannot leave a child behind by forgetting about it. Output capture is always on, whatever *output* says, so a stopped child still reports what the command wrote.",
