          },
          {
            "name": "result",
            "kind": "property",
            "display": "result: CommandResult | None",
            "doc": {
              "summary": "The settled outcome, or <code>None</code> while the command is still running.",
              "sections": [
                {
                  "title": "Returns",
                  "fields": [
                    {
                      "name": "",
                      "type": "CommandResult | None",
                      "description": "The command's result once settlement has completed, otherwise <code>None</code>. The property never waits; use <code>wait</code> to block until there is an outcome to read. A wait whose deadline elapsed publishes the outcome here too, because the child it stopped is nonetheless reaped and has one."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "wait",
            "kind": "method",
            "display": "async def wait(*, timeout: float | None = None) -> CommandResult",
            "doc": {
              "summary": "Wait for the command to finish and return its outcome.",
              "body": [
                "The first caller to arrive settles the run; every later caller awaits the same settlement and sees the same outcome, so calling this repeatedly or concurrently is safe and reports one result."
              ],
              "sections": [
                {
                  "title": "Parameters",
                  "fields": [
                    {
                      "name": "timeout",
                      "type": "float | None, default=None",
                      "description": "Seconds to allow the command to finish. Expiry stops the child the way a timed-out <code>run()</code> does and raises <a href=\"/cuprum/docs/api/errors/#TimeoutExpired\"><code>TimeoutExpired</code></a> carrying the output captured before the deadline. <code>None</code> falls back to the deadline <a href=\"/cuprum/docs/api/commands/#SafeCmd\"><code>SafeCmd.start</code></a> resolved for this handle, and to no deadline at all when <code>start()</code> resolved none."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "title": "Returns",
                  "fields": [
                    {
                      "name": "",
                      "type": "CommandResult",
                      "description": "The command's outcome once it has exited."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "title": "Raises",
                  "fields": [
                    {
                      "name": "TimeoutExpired",
                      "type": "",
                      "description": "If *timeout*, or the deadline <code>start()</code> resolved, elapsed before the command finished."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "signal",
            "kind": "method",
            "display": "async def signal(signal_number: int) -> None",
            "doc": {
              "summary": "Deliver a POSIX signal to the running command.",
              "body": [
                "Unlike <code>terminate</code> and <code>kill</code>, this asks for exactly the signal named and takes no view on how the child should respond. It does not settle the run: a child sent <code>SIGSTOP</code>, or sent a signal it ignores, is still the caller's to wait on or stop."
              ],
              "sections": [
                {
                  "title": "Parameters",
                  "fields": [
                    {
                      "name": "signal_number",
                      "type": "int",
                      "description": "The signal to deliver, as <code>signal</code> spells it."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "title": "Raises",
                  "fields": [
                    {
                      "name": "SignalAfterExitError",
                      "type": "",
                      "description": "If the command has already exited, carrying its exit code."
                    },
                    {
                      "name": "UnsupportedSignalError",
                      "type": "",
                      "description": "If the platform cannot deliver a caller-named signal."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "terminate",
            "kind": "method",
            "display": "async def terminate(*, grace: float | None = None) -> CommandResult",
            "doc": {
              "summary": "Stop the command gracefully, escalating if it does not comply.",
              "body": [
                "The child is sent <code>SIGTERM</code>, given *grace* seconds, then sent <code>SIGKILL</code> if it is still there. Both the signal that ended it and the output it produced before ending are preserved: a child that exited on the <code>SIGTERM</code> reports <code>-15</code>, and one that had to be killed reports <code>-9</code>.",
                "Calling this on a command that has already exited is a no-op that reports the recorded outcome — including when a <code>wait</code> deadline is what ended the child, since the outcome that wait produced is the one this returns."
              ],
              "sections": [
                {
                  "title": "Parameters",
                  "fields": [
                    {
                      "name": "grace",
                      "type": "float | None, default=None",
                      "description": "Seconds to wait between the graceful signal and the forced one. Defaults to the execution context's cancel grace, which is the same window a cancelled <code>run()</code> allows."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "title": "Returns",
                  "fields": [
                    {
                      "name": "",
                      "type": "CommandResult",
                      "description": "The ended command's outcome."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "kill",
            "kind": "method",
            "display": "async def kill() -> CommandResult",
            "doc": {
              "summary": "Stop the command immediately, without a grace period.",
              "body": [
                "This is the forced half of <code>terminate</code> on its own: the child is sent <code>SIGKILL</code> and reaped, so its outcome reports <code>-9</code> unless it had already exited, in which case the recorded outcome is returned. Unlike <code>terminate</code>, no <code>SIGTERM</code> is sent first, so the reported signal is the one the caller asked for rather than whichever one happened to end the child."
              ],
              "sections": [
                {
                  "title": "Returns",
                  "fields": [
                    {
                      "name": "",
                      "type": "CommandResult",
                      "description": "The ended command's outcome."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
