      {
        "name": "cuprum.adapters.echo_metrics",
        "kind": "module",
        "module": "cuprum.adapters.echo_metrics",
        "path": "cuprum/adapters/echo_metrics.py",
        "line": 1,
        "display": "from cuprum.adapters import echo_metrics",
        "doc": {
          "summary": "Metrics adapter for stream-echo failure and truncation events.",
          "body": [
            "Counts how often a text-only echo sink rejected the subprocess output, per output stream, and how often a bounded echoed line was successfully truncated. Those facts are otherwise visible only through a <code>WARNING</code> log record or the echo observation hook, which dashboards cannot aggregate.",
            "The hook consumes <a href=\"/cuprum/docs/api/observation/#EchoEvent\"><code>EchoEvent</code></a> values from <a href=\"/cuprum/docs/api/observation/#observe_echo\"><code>observe_echo</code></a>. It reuses the <code>MetricsCollector</code> protocol, so one collector can back the execution, pump, and echo hooks and no new telemetry dependency is introduced."
          ],
          "examples": "::\n\n    from cuprum import sh\n    from cuprum.adapters.echo_metrics import EchoMetricsHook\n    from cuprum.adapters.metrics_adapter import InMemoryMetrics\n    from cuprum.echo_observation import observe_echo\n\n    metrics = InMemoryMetrics()\n\n    with sh.observe(MetricsHook(metrics)), observe_echo(EchoMetricsHook(metrics)):\n        command.run_sync(output=RunOutputOptions(echo=True))\n\n    print(metrics.counters[\"cuprum_echo_encoding_failures_total\"])"
        },
        "members": [
          {
            "name": "ECHO_BROKEN_PIPE_TOTAL",
            "kind": "constant",
            "display": "ECHO_BROKEN_PIPE_TOTAL = 'cuprum_echo_broken_pipe_total'",
            "doc": {
              "summary": "Echo writes abandoned after <code>BrokenPipeError</code>, labelled by <code>stream</code>.",
              "body": [
                "A distinct series from <code>ECHO_ENCODING_FAILURES_TOTAL</code>: both count a handled echo disablement, but they report different faults with different remedies. An encoding failure is inherent to the sink's configuration and recurs for every run that reaches it; a broken pipe means a destination that was expected to stay open did not, which is exactly the signal an operator wants to alert on separately. Folding them together would make a permanently misencoded sink indistinguishable from a downstream reader that keeps disconnecting.",
                "Only recorded when the caller opted in with <code>BEST_EFFORT</code>; under the default policy the error propagates and no event is emitted."
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "ECHO_ENCODING_FAILURES_TOTAL",
            "kind": "constant",
            "display": "ECHO_ENCODING_FAILURES_TOTAL = 'cuprum_echo_encoding_failures_total'",
            "doc": {
              "summary": "Echo writes rejected with <code>UnicodeEncodeError</code>, labelled by <code>stream</code>.",
              "body": [
                "The only other label is <code>error_category</code>, whose single value (<code>UNICODE_ENCODE</code>) names the closed category the counter counts. The label exists so a future failure category extends the metric rather than silently mixing into this series — which is what <code>ECHO_BROKEN_PIPE_TOTAL</code> then did."
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "ECHO_TRUNCATIONS_TOTAL",
            "kind": "constant",
            "display": "ECHO_TRUNCATIONS_TOTAL = 'cuprum_echo_truncations_total'",
            "doc": {
              "summary": "Successfully written bounded echo lines, labelled by <code>stream</code>."
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "EchoMetricsHook",
            "kind": "class",
            "display": "class EchoMetricsHook(collector: MetricsCollector) -> None",
            "doc": {
              "summary": "Echo observation hook that records bounded echo outcomes.",
              "body": [
                "The hook emits <code>cuprum_echo_encoding_failures_total</code>: incremented once per first <code>UnicodeEncodeError</code> on a drain's echo path, labelled <code>stream</code> with <code>stdout</code> or <code>stderr</code> and <code>error_category</code> with <code>unicode_encode</code>. It also emits <code>cuprum_echo_truncations_total</code> once per successfully written truncation, labelled only by <code>stream</code>.",
                "A <code>BrokenPipeError</code> the caller chose to tolerate under <code>BEST_EFFORT</code> increments <code>cuprum_echo_broken_pipe_total</code> instead, with the same label set and <code>error_category</code> of <code>broken_pipe</code>. It is a separate series, so a sink that cannot encode is never confused with a destination that keeps closing.",
                "A drain that has already disabled echo emits nothing further, so repeated chunks after the first failure do not compound the count."
              ],
              "sections": [
                {
                  "title": "Parameters",
